# rk3588 `vendor-patched` — symbols Armbian's published .config declares that
# CANNOT exist in the pinned kernel tree.
#
# Consumed by lib/verify-kernel-config.sh as its optional <allow-absent> list,
# wired in by kernel_source.config_absent_symbols in families/rk3588.yaml.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# The `vendor-patched` variant starts from Armbian's own complete
# config/kernel/linux-rk35xx-vendor.config — the exact config the shipped
# linux-image-vendor-rk35xx is built with — because a bare `make defconfig`
# would produce a materially different driver set and make any comparison
# against the running board meaningless.
#
# But that config is written for a tree Armbian has already MUTATED. Armbian's
# `EXTRAWIFI` step (lib/functions/compilation/patch/drivers_network.sh,
# `driver_rtl8189ES`, `driver_rtw88`, `driver_rtl8852bs`, `driver_uwe5622`, …)
# COPIES whole out-of-tree WiFi/BT driver source trees into
# drivers/net/wireless/ and appends their Kconfig/Makefile entries, at build
# time, before configuring. None of that source is in armbian/linux-rockchip.
#
# This pipeline deliberately does NOT invoke the Armbian build framework (see
# lib/build-kernel.sh's header: adopting it would make "what exactly is in this
# kernel" unanswerable from this repo). So these symbols have no Kconfig entry
# in the pinned tree, `olddefconfig` discards them, and the survival gate
# correctly reports every one of them.
#
# Each entry below is therefore a reviewed statement of fact: "this symbol names
# an out-of-tree driver Armbian injects and we do not."
#
# NOT AN ESCAPE HATCH. verify-kernel-config.sh fails the build if a symbol
# listed here DID survive — a stale entry is an error, not a silent no-op — so
# this list cannot quietly grow into a blanket opt-out of the gate.
#
# NEITHER SHIPPED BOARD NEEDS ANY OF THESE. Rock 5B+ WiFi is the RTL8852BE,
# whose driver is IN-TREE and resolves CONFIG_RTW89=m / CONFIG_RTW89_8852BE=m;
# Orange Pi 5+ is the AP6275P on in-tree CONFIG_BRCMFMAC=m. Both survive the
# gate. Adding a board whose adapter IS on this list means adding the driver
# source, not extending this file.

# --- Realtek rtw88 SDIO/USB variants ---------------------------------------
# In-tree rtw88 in 6.1 carries only the PCIe parts (8822BE/8822CE/8723DE/
# 8821CE). The SDIO and USB variants below come from Armbian's `driver_rtw88`.
CONFIG_RTW88_8822BS
CONFIG_RTW88_8822BU
CONFIG_RTW88_8822CS
CONFIG_RTW88_8822CU
CONFIG_RTW88_8723DS
CONFIG_RTW88_8723DU
CONFIG_RTW88_8821CS
CONFIG_RTW88_8821CU

# --- standalone out-of-tree Realtek vendor drivers --------------------------
# Each is a separate vendor source tree Armbian clones and copies in.
CONFIG_RTL8852BS
CONFIG_RTL8723DS
CONFIG_RTL8822BU
CONFIG_RTL8821CU
CONFIG_88XXAU
CONFIG_RTL8192EU
CONFIG_RTL8189ES

# --- UNISOC/Spreadtrum UWE5622 combo WiFi+BT (driver_uwe5622) ---------------
CONFIG_SC23XX
CONFIG_UMW2653
CONFIG_SC2342_INTEG
CONFIG_SC2355
CONFIG_SC2366
CONFIG_SPARD_WLAN_SUPPORT
CONFIG_WLAN_UWE5622
CONFIG_UNISOC_WIFI_PS
CONFIG_TTY_OVERY_SDIO
